/// Origin of a deck-add event. Listeners may branch on this; the bus
/// itself is source-agnostic.
///
/// Mirrors Python's implicit add-site taxonomy at `01c094d`:
///   * `Reward` — normal card-reward pick after combat
///     (`run_state.py::add_card_reward`).
///   * `EventGain` — event-room "you get a card" path.
///   * `RelicGain` — a relic synthesized the card into the deck.
///   * `BingBongDuplicate` — re-entry from
///     [`crate::CombatState::duplicate_last_added_card`].
///     `BingBong`-style listeners filter on this to break the
///     infinite-recursion loop (replaces Python's `_skip_next` field
///     at `shop_event.py:828-836`).
///   * `ShopPurchase` — bought from the merchant.
///   * `Other` — catch-all for synthetic / test / debug adds.
///
/// TODO bead `sts2-rs-01o`: `BingBong`'s body lands here in the umbrella
/// retrofit; the body checks `ctx.source != AddSource::BingBongDuplicate`
/// as its primary re-entry guard.
#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Hash)]
pub enum AddSource {
    /// Post-combat card-reward pick.
    Reward,
    /// Event-room "you get a card" outcome.
    EventGain,
    /// A relic synthesized the card into the deck.
    RelicGain,
    /// Re-entry from
    /// [`crate::CombatState::duplicate_last_added_card`].
    BingBongDuplicate,
    /// Bought from the merchant / shop.
    ShopPurchase,
    /// Catch-all: synthetic / test / debug add.
    Other,
}

